# Everything in this directory is published to https://github.com/Anode1/articles.
# Anything that must not be published (drafts, emails, endorsement letters, credentials)
# lives in a PRIVATE/ directory beside the work it belongs to; git never sees those.
# Only `git add -f` can override the rule, so never use it in this tree.

# LaTeX build artifacts
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.bcf
*.run.xml
*.blg
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.bak
*.bak2
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Per-generation run data behind the emergence paper. Not build logs.
!smbpann/data/*.log

# Credentials, as a backstop. Nothing matching this should ever be in this tree.
.apikey
*.key

# Local agent config, not content.
.claude/

# Python venvs for the measurement scripts. Recreate with the pinned versions in each paper.
venv/

# Private: how Vasili writes. Kept on disk, never published.
STYLE.md

# Private material beside the work: emails, drafts, letters, keys. Never published.
PRIVATE/
